<title>USA: US Stockpile sells 2,828 tonnes of zinc.</title>
<headline>US Stockpile sells 2,828 tonnes of zinc.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 6,235,000 lbs (2,828 tonnes) of zinc for $3,727,428 at an average price of 59.78 cents a lb.</p>
<p>The winning bidders were Commercial Alloys, Sipi Metals, Ingot Metal Co, Tally Metal Sales, Hochschild Partners, Trademet, Parks-Pioneer, Sogem-Afrimet, and American Alloys.</p>
<p>The metal offered was a mix of prime western and high grade.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
